.\" Revised Draft prepared from current source; see EDITORS-NOTES.md.
.\" Source: src/tune.c
.TH "TUNE" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
tune \- set or query a radiod channel from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tune
.RI "[options] -s ssrc [-r radio | radio]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
tune sends a tagged command to one radiod channel, waits for matching status,
prints reported settings, and exits. An unknown nonreserved SSRC can create a
dynamic channel if radiod has a usable template. With no parameter changes it
queries the channel, but still sends the lifetime setting, which defaults to
zero. A matching command tag confirms receipt, not acceptance of every
requested setting. Unsupported or invalid settings may be ignored. Other
controllers can change the same channel.

Note that there is no retry limit on commands if the radiod server does not respond.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-r radio, \-\-radio radio"
Select the control/status destination. A positional argument or RADIO may
supply it instead.
.TP
.B "\-s ssrc, \-\-ssrc ssrc"
Select the channel SSRC. Required; zero is reserved.
.TP
.B "\-f frequency, \-\-frequency frequency"
Set carrier frequency. An explicit SI suffix is recommended, for example 10m
or 147m435; unscaled values use the radio-frequency parser heuristic.
.TP
.B "\-m preset, \-\-mode preset"
Apply a named preset from the server presets file. Other parameters in the
command override preset settings.
.TP
.B "\-R rate, \-\-samprate rate"
Set output sample rate in Hz; SI suffixes are accepted. The server must
support the requested rate.
.TP
.B "\-L frequency, \-\-low frequency"
Set lower filter edge in Hz relative to the tuned carrier. Use an equals form
such as --low=-3000 for a negative long-option argument.
.TP
.B "\-H frequency, \-\-high frequency"
Set upper filter edge in Hz relative to the tuned carrier.
.TP
.B "\-g dB, \-\-gain dB"
Set output gain and disable channel AGC. Takes precedence over --agc in the
same invocation.
.TP
.B "\-a, \-\-agc"
Enable channel AGC unless --gain is also given.
.TP
.B "\-G dB, \-\-rfgain dB, \-\-fegain dB"
Request frontend RF gain. This is shared hardware state and can affect other
channels.
.TP
.B "\-A dB, \-\-rfatten dB, \-\-featten dB"
Request frontend attenuation, where supported.
.TP
.B "\-e encoding, \-\-encoding encoding"
Set output encoding. Common values include s16le, s16be, f32le, f16le, opus,
and opus-voip. The server and sample rate must support the selection.
.TP
.B "\-D destination, \-\-destination destination"
Set output data destination; default destination port is 5004.
.TP
.B "\-b frames, \-\-buffer frames"
Set output aggregation delay in radiod frames, subject to server limits.
.TP
.B "\-t frames, \-\-lifetime frames"
Set channel lifetime in processing frames.
Ordinary commands refresh the channel lifetime.
.TP
.B "\-w rate, \-\-sweep\-rate rate"
Set frequency sweep rate in Hz/s. Positive values sweep upward.
.TP
.B "\-S seconds, \-\-sweep\-start seconds"
Set relative sweep start time in seconds.
.TP
.B "\-d seconds, \-\-sweep\-duration seconds"
Set sweep duration in seconds.
.TP
.B "\-p seconds, \-\-sweep\-period seconds"
Set sweep repetition period in seconds. Zero-valued sweep options are
currently omitted from the command.
.TP
.B "\-i interface, \-\-iface interface"
Select the multicast interface.
.TP
.B "\-o source, \-\-source source"
Restrict received status to the selected network source. This does not select
an SSRC.
.TP
.B "\-l locale, \-\-locale locale"
Select display locale.
.TP
.B "\-q, \-\-quiet"
Suppress the normal status summary.
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-verbose"
Increase diagnostics; may be repeated.
.TP
.B "\-V, \-\-version"
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B "\-h, \-\-help"
Print usage. The current implementation exits with usage-error status.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
RADIO supplies the control destination when it is not given on the command
line. LANG supplies the initial locale.
.SH EXAMPLES
Query a channel, then apply an AM preset and tune it:
.PP
.nf
tune \-r hf.local \-s 10000000
tune \-r hf.local \-s 10000000 \-m am \-f 10m
.fi
.SH NOTES
The program retries commands while waiting for matching status and has no
overall response timeout. It may wait indefinitely if the server cannot be
reached. Zero-valued sweep requests cannot currently clear an existing sweep
setting.
.SH SEE ALSO
radiod(8), control(1), metadump(1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
